        "response": {
          "output": "Not broken. The `agent` RPC is async by design. It returns `{ runId, acceptedAt }` right away and the run continues in the background.\n\nTo get the answer:\n- **Call `agent.wait` with that `runId`.** It resolves with `ok`, `error` or `timeout` when the run ends.\n- **Or listen on the same WebSocket.** `assistant`, `tool` and `lifecycle` events stream in as the run proceeds.\n\n`agent.wait` only observes the run, and its timeout doesn't stop the run. To cancel, use `sessions.abort` (or `chat.abort` for a queued turn).\n\nIf `agent.wait` returns `error` or `timeout`, or the run never starts, send me the `runId` and the `lifecycle` events. A busy session can also delay a run, because runs are serialized per session. I took this from the skill docs and didn't check your code or logs."
        },
