        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nHow does one agent hand work to a sub-agent?",
          "label": "evals/openclaw-agents/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "83a194643e6f574b10dd0ccf96df566d05bba810ad9059c0c3a534543d10ed19",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "In OpenClaw, a parent agent hands work to a sub-agent by calling the `sessions_spawn` tool. It starts an isolated background sub-agent run and returns a run id right away. The parent then calls `sessions_yield` to end its turn, and the sub-agent's result is pushed back to it. Don't poll `subagents` or `sessions_list` for completion.\n\n- **Isolation:** the sub-agent gets a minimal system prompt. It has no session or message tools unless you opt into an orchestrator pattern.\n- **Config:** `agents.defaults.subagents` holds `delegationMode`, `maxSpawnDepth` (default 1) and `maxConcurrent`. `delegationMode: \"prefer\"` only changes the prompt, not which tools are available.\n- **Concurrency:** sub-agents run in their own `subagent` lane, capped at 8.\n\nI couldn't search this repo because the file-search tools were disabled in this session. This answer comes from the `openclaw-agents` skill. Details are in `references/agents-config.md` under that skill.\n\nIf you meant the SDLC team in this toolkit, where `sdlc-orchestrator` hands work to the dev pair, tell me and I'll look at that instead."
        },
